-5ad4-4ac4-bc6d-b835ccd6cc1d","position":{"commit_sha":"dc10a8a4391ceddb1283a6d5106267c838770c9c","position":"1785434832273700523-1b1cc33e-5ad4-4ac4-bc6d-b835ccd6cc1d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"d1ad70ed-ce91-4b63-9f32-e6b36aea17d4","comments":[],"created_at":1785384380449166001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2412b80b-e13d-4664-ab2e-8bc309098b4f","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"4ee2-3baa-be5c-488d"},{"link_uuid":"38a02518-5f07-4499-93b0-2e9b5ec1f96e","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"49b8-0c3a-53c3-46ad"},{"link_uuid":"614764ef-f1a7-41da-9240-661215d2278e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"29ba-ac6c-bc2a-4313"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nT3 (integration feasibility) and T10 (infra/IaC) have never blocked in ~2,500 runs each — a configuration artifact, not a quality signal: 13/20 sampled T3 findings were actionable codebase-grounded criticisms and 62% of T10's strong findings cite concrete repo artifacts. The audited T10 keyword gate measured 28% fire rate with 100% strong-finding recall. Operator approved enabling blocking for both. Plan-review blocking is derived from `default_posture: \"blocking\"` plus `block_threshold` in the routing entry (the `blocking_enabled` field is the code-review gate's convention and does not apply here), and there is no per-class blocking mechanism in Pass-3 — a finding blocks when its criterion is blocking-postured and its priority crosses the threshold.\n\n## Approach\n(1) In src/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json set `default_posture: \"blocking\"` with `block_threshold: 0.90` for T3 and T10 (conservative pilot; the standing zero-LLM criterion-effectiveness recorder monitors outcomes for a later 0.85 revisit). (2) Class scoping for T10 is achieved through severity guidance, not a new mechanism: one sentence added to src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_T10.md stating that only its MAJOR classes (destructive apply, wildcard/overbroad grant, plaintext secret on a committed path, unauthenticated internet-reachable service) warrant severity >= major — so lesser findings cannot reach the 0.90 priority threshold through the existing severity->priority pipeline. No pass3_decide changes. (3) The T10 DET overlay gate is added as a DetGateRule in src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_gate_rules.py (the established home for trigger vocabularies since change 1041), transcribed verbatim from the audit: text_all[0] = `\\b(?:terraform|cloudformation|pulumi|ansible|kubernetes|helm|k8s|iac|aws|ec2|s3|iam|ssm|cloudwatch|vpc|sns|lambda|rds|ebs|docker|compose|infra/|provision\\w*|systemd|launchagent|user_data|cloudfront|api gateway|oidc|\\.github/workflows|github actions|workflow_dispatch|pull_request_target|secrets\\.[A-Z_]+)\\b` (case-insensitive), no file_impact arms. (4) tests/unit/test_threshold_recalibration.py contains TWO assertions that pin the blocking configuration and BOTH are updated in the same commit: the pinned full-routing-table assertion (test_full_routing_table_matches_pinned_expectation) gains the two posture changes, and the blocking-set assertion (test_only_the_approved_and_prerequisite_criteria_are_blocking) has T3 and T10 added to its hardcoded approved blocking set. (5) docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md regenerated with the documented command. Alternative rejected: enabling at 0.85 immediately — 0.90 first bounds the blast radius while the effectiveness recorder accumulates post-change data at zero LLM cost; and building a per-class blocking mechanism in Pass-3 — new machinery when severity guidance reaches the same outcome through the existing pipeline.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_gate_rules.py, src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_T10.md, tests/unit/test_threshold_recalibration.py (update pinned table), tests/unit/plan_review/test_criteria_blocking.py (new), docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md (regenerated).\n\n## Testing\nUnit (relative imports): a T3 finding at priority 0.92 produces a blocking decision through Pass-3 and one at 0.85 stays advisory; same for a T10 fixture; the T10 DetGateRule fires on a terraform-touching fixture plan and a GHA workflow plan and skips a pure-docs plan with a routing.det_gated coverage entry and zero T10 LLM routing; the updated pinned routing table matches; the T10 rubric contains the severity-guidance sentence.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] T3 and T10 carry default_posture blocking with block_threshold 0.90 and findings above/below the threshold block/stay-advisory through Pass-3 (checked: `pytest tests/unit/plan_review/test_criteria_blocking.py`).\n- [ ] The T10 DetGateRule fires on infra and GHA fixtures and skips non-infra plans with a det_gated coverage entry (checked: unit tests).\n- [ ] plan_review_T10.md contains the MAJOR-class severity-guidance sentence (checked: rubric text assertion).\n- [ ] Both pinned assertions in test_threshold_recalibration.py — the full routing table and the approved-blocking-criteria set — reflect T3/T10 and the whole file passes (checked: `pytest tests/unit/test_threshold_recalibration.py`).\n- [ ] The criteria guide is regenerated (checked: committed regen output).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json","reason":"T3/T10 blocking posture"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_gate_rules.py","reason":"T10 DetGateRule"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_T10.md","reason":"MAJOR-class severity guidance"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_threshold_recalibration.py","reason":"pinned table update"},{"path":"tests/unit/plan_review/test_criteria_blocking.py","reason":"new tests"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md","reason":"regenerated"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","49b8-0c3a-53c3-46ad"],["depends_on","4ee2-3baa-be5c-488d"],["parent","a492-3e46-ca44-40a5"],["relates_to","29ba-ac6c-bc2a-4313"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"a492-3e46-ca44-40a5","parent_status_uuid":"0dd67ecf-b12a-43a4-b982-ec941218819e","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"bfa8-51d0-3286-4779","ticket_type":"story","title":"Enable T3 and T10 blocking and add the T10 infra DET overlay gate","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b80c68cf-9dba-439d-acbe-ac0a82c9a7de","234d01d9-a3f8-44a9-9110-1e33674349d8","2412b80b-e13d-4664-ab2e-8bc309098b4f","38a02518-5f07-4499-93b0-2e9b5ec1f96e","c0476cf8-efda-4572-9d04-1ab89903add6","3d38aa7a-b521-4ec0-9908-ed657e39e56a","90f8d911-03bc-4657-9dbc-1614e367a947","05ddd4dd-e9d1-4ed4-871e-fd0c838483e3","0dd67ecf-b12a-43a4-b982-ec941218819e","cb62effe-1172-418a-a7b4-860f6f82349f","1b1cc33e-5ad4-4ac4-bc6d-b835ccd6cc1d","614764ef-f1a7-41da-9240-661215d2278e"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785436679120455197,"uuid":"8babce49-1732-4da5-a1ae-d2b221b5d362"}